CAVEAT:  This run did not establish the following.
         1. The per-destination command `log host <ip> facility <f>` does not override
            the facility. It selects which messages are sent. STEP 3 shows the proof.
            So two collectors cannot be given two different facilities on this platform.
            The requirement is met by the global `log facility` command only.
         2. Only one facility value was set globally (local4). The other 19 values the
            CLI offers were not measured.
         3. The collector was a packet capture on the testbox, not a syslog server. This
            run proves what the DUT put on the wire. It does not prove what a syslog
            server would store.
         4. Secure logging over TLS (`log host <ip> secure`) was not tested.
         5. The run used one DUT in a standalone (not stacked) configuration.
